.TH CROC 1 "" "croc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
croc \- transfer files, directories, and text using a short code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B croc
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B croc send
.RI [ options ] " file ..."
.br
.B croc store
.RI [ options ] " file ..."
.br
.B croc ssh
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B croc sync
.RI [ options ] " folder"
.br
.B croc relay
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Croc transfers data between computers using a shared code. Connections are
encrypted end to end, with direct connections when available and relay fallback.
Both participants must be available for a normal transfer. The store command
uploads encrypted regular files for later retrieval. The sync command keeps a
folder synchronized one-way from a source computer to a destination computer,
transferring only new or changed files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a file:
.PP
.RS
.B croc send document.pdf
.RE
.PP
Receive a file by running croc and entering the code at its prompt:
.PP
.RS
.B croc
.RE
.PP
Sync a folder one-way from the source computer:
.PP
.RS
.B croc sync ./project
.RE
.PP
Receive synced changes on the destination computer (previewing deletions first):
.PP
.RS
.B CROC_SECRET='code-phrase' croc sync --dry-run --delete ./project
.RE
.PP
Watch the source folder and sync edits continuously:
.PP
.RS
.B croc sync --watch ./project
.RE
.PP
On Unix, a code may also be passed using the CROC_SECRET environment variable.
Avoid putting secrets in command arguments or shell history.
.PP
Show all options for a command:
.PP
.RS
.B croc send --help
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send
Send files, directories, or text. Use --transport auto, derp, or relay to select
the file data transport. Use --zip to send a directory as an archive.
.TP
.B store
Upload client-side encrypted regular files for later download. Use --help for
expiration, download-limit, and storage service options.
.TP
.B ssh
Share an interactive terminal using separate read/write and read-only invitations.
An invitation grants the access described by the host until the session ends.
.TP
.B sync
Keep a folder synchronized one-way from a source computer to a destination
computer. Both sides require
.I folder
to already exist as a directory.
The role is determined by the
.B CROC_SECRET
environment variable: run without
.B CROC_SECRET
on the source computer, and set
.B CROC_SECRET
on the destination computer. Passing flags belonging to the opposite role exits
with status 1.
.RS
.PP
Source flags (without CROC_SECRET):
.TP
.B --code, -c CODE
Use a custom code phrase (at least 6 characters). On Unix, requires classic mode
(\fBcroc --classic\fR) to avoid exposing secrets in the process list.
.TP
.B --transport MODE
Select the file data transport: \fBauto\fR (default), \fBderp\fR, or \fBrelay\fR.
.TP
.B --exclude STRINGS
Exclude paths containing any of the comma-separated substrings (case-insensitive).
.TP
.B --exclude-file PATHS
Exclude exact comma-separated relative paths.
.TP
.B --git
Respect \fB.gitignore\fR rules and skip Git-ignored entries.
.TP
.B --qrcode, --qr
Display a QR code for the Web Sync URL (\fB<web-url>/?sync=<code>#sync\fR).
Cannot be combined with \fB--transport derp\fR.
.TP
.B --watch
Watch the source folder and continuously sync changes over a single session
until interrupted with Ctrl-C. The destination follows watch mode automatically.
.TP
.B --no-local
Disable local relay and LAN discovery.
.PP
Destination flags (with CROC_SECRET set):
.TP
.B --delete
Delete destination files and directories absent from the source, subject to
safety checks (incomplete source scans, filtered/skipped entries, empty source,
and >50% file-deletion confirmation).
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the planned changes without downloading files or modifying the destination.
.TP
.B --checksum
Compare file contents with xxhash64 even when size and modification time match.
.TP
.B --allow-empty-source
Allow \fB--delete\fR to delete destination entries when the source folder is empty.
.RE
.TP
.B relay
Run a relay explicitly. Installing this package does not start a relay service.
.TP
.B update
Install or refresh the adjacent croc-update utility, then print the command to
update croc. Direct croc-update use selects croc from PATH, falling back to an
installation beside the updater when absent. Use --path EXECUTABLE to select
a particular croc, including a user-owned Go bin installation.
Both commands accept --check to report availability without installation and
--yes to skip confirmation. Protected locations may require sudo/doas or
Windows UAC authentication. Package-managed installations must be updated
with their owning package manager.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help, -h
Show usage and the complete list of options. Each subcommand has its own help.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Print the installed release version.
.TP
.B --yes
Automatically accept prompts. Use only when the sender and transfer are trusted.
In \fBcroc sync\fR, does not bypass the typed \fByes\fR confirmation required
when deleting more than half of the destination files.
.TP
.B --out DIRECTORY
Receive files in DIRECTORY.
.TP
.B --relay ADDRESS
Use the specified relay.
.TP
.B --pass PASSWORD
Password for the relay (or path to a file containing the password).
.TP
.B --web-url URL
Web client origin for receive and Web Sync links and QR codes.
.TP
.B --quiet
Disable output (in \fBcroc sync --dry-run\fR, the plan is still printed).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully (including \fBcroc sync\fR when already in sync,
\fB--dry-run\fR completion, or stopping \fBcroc sync --watch\fR with Ctrl-C).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (invalid flags or role mismatch, missing folder, network/PAKE/protocol
error, peer lacking \fBfolder-sync-v1\fR, non-interactive \fB--delete\fR without
\fB--yes\fR in one-shot sync, or Ctrl-C interruption in one-shot sync).
.TP
.B 2
Partial completion in one-shot \fBcroc sync\fR: one or more items failed to
commit or delete, conflicts occurred, or deletions were held (for example,
unconfirmed >50% deletions or commit failures).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CROC_SECRET
The code or invitation used for a transfer or shared terminal. For
.BR "croc sync" ,
setting
.B CROC_SECRET
selects the destination role; leaving it unset selects the source role.
.TP
.B CROC_CONFIG_DIR
Override the per-user configuration directory.
.SH FILES
Croc keeps per-user configuration separately from the package installation.
Removing or upgrading this package does not remove transferred files or user
configuration.
.SH SECURITY
Share codes only with intended recipients. Check the transfer description before
accepting files and use a dedicated output directory when receiving untrusted
content. See the project security policy to report vulnerabilities privately.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/schollz/croc
Project documentation and release notes
.UE
